# Nothing here is about tidiness. Every line is something that must not be
# published, and there was no .gitignore at all until the operator pointed out
# he intends to share this repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- other people
# Fetched comment sections. Hundreds of real YouTube users' display names and
# their words, gathered to build one packet. It is not ours to republish, and
# it is the single largest thing in this tree.
output/
ab_compare/
previous_runs/
packets_for_review.zip

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- the operator
# His own drafts and what he did with them. This is measurement data, not
# code, and it is irreplaceable -- ignoring it here keeps it off GitHub, it
# does NOT delete it and nothing in this project ever should.
posted_history.json
engagement_history.sqlite3
replies_to_review.md
comment_drafts.md

# Settings resolve from the user config directory, but a local override file
# would carry a handle, an output path, possibly a proxy with credentials in
# the URL.
youtube_packet_settings.json
window_settings.json
settings.json
.env

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
# The API key lives in the environment. These exist so that a key written to a
# file by mistake does not become a commit.
*.key
YOUTUBE_API_KEY.txt
*api_key*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Whisper model downloads and the audio it transcribes. Large, re-derivable,
# and the audio is somebody else's video.
models/
*.m4a
*.webm
*.mp3
*.wav

# Editors and Windows
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
